Actually, it currently tells that POST requests are uncached completely. And this is not true, since you can opt-out of this behavior by adding `cache: "force-cache` to your `fetch.options`.

A valid use case is the usage of GraphQL where each request is an HTTP POST request by default.

Also, it should be documented in the [`fetch options.cache`](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/caching#opting-out-1) documentation, that it's possible to use `force-cache` to make POST requests cached via data cache.
